<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Thera</h1><p class="st-meta">900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.) · capital Thera</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Dorian island city on volcanic Santorini, best known as the founder of Cyrene in Libya and for some of the earliest Greek inscriptions.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> eruption destroyed the Minoan town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akrotiri-prehistoric-city">Akrotiri</a>, Santorini was resettled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorians">Dorians</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laconia">Laconia</a> in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>, led by tradition by Theras. Their town grew on the ridge of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesa-vouno">Mesa Vouno</a>, on the south-east of the island.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Thera was an aristocratic community with Spartan customs, and its rock-cut inscriptions of the 7th century BCE are among the oldest Greek writing. On Delphi's advice, Therans sent settlers under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battus-i-of-cyrene">Battus</a> to found <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cyrene">Cyrene</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> c. 631 BCE, as recorded in a later foundation decree. The island paid tribute to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a> in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/delian-league">Delian League</a> from the 420s BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 3rd century BCE Thera became a Ptolemaic naval base, with a garrison and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gymnasium">gymnasium</a>. It passed under Roman control by 146 BCE, and its ancient city on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesa-vouno">Mesa Vouno</a> remained inhabited into Byzantine times.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:41.79%;width:15.00%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thera</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion; cult of Apollo Karneios</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Doric Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Santorini</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-523&amp;focus=thera" aria-label="Thera on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5320 864 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Thera lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5640 1120L5591 1068M5640 1120L5772 1297"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5591 1068h0M5772 1297h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5640 1120h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5640 1120h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-523&amp;focus=thera">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

